WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.767
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.323
This lesson covers objective 2 point 1.

00:00:10.323 --> 00:00:13.468
Explain characteristics of routing technologies.

00:00:13.468 --> 00:00:18.580
Today's concept: when two routes disagree, what does the router compare first?

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.433
A router learns a default route two ways.

00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:26.646
One is typed in by an administrator, a static route.

00:00:26.646 --> 00:00:28.500
The other is learned from RIP.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.387
RIP shows a lower metric, just one hop.

00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:33.551
That tempts people to choose RIP.

00:00:33.551 --> 00:00:36.960
But the router does not compare those numbers first.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.328
First it compares administrative distance, which measures how much the router trusts the source.

00:00:45.328 --> 00:00:46.207
Static is one.

00:00:46.207 --> 00:00:47.840
RIP is one hundred twenty.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.947
One is lower than one hundred twenty, so the static route is installed.

00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:54.980
The decision is made before the metric is ever looked at.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:02.590
Metric only matters when two routes come from the same protocol, such as two RIP paths with one hop and three hops.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:10.476
For the exam, administrative distance decides between route sources, and the lowest one wins.

00:01:10.476 --> 00:01:14.411
Metric is only used to choose among routes from the same protocol.

00:01:14.411 --> 00:01:16.260
That's objective two point one.
